{% include "css/ice-type.css" %}
</style>

{{ iceIntro | safe }}

<figure
  class="phase-poem"
  aria-label="Concrete poem about an ice cube absorbing energy and melting"
>
  <div class="phase-poem-art" aria-hidden="true">
    <p class="phase-poem-label">
      <span>PHASE STUDY / ONE CUBE</span>
      <span>&minus;5&deg;C &rarr; 0&deg;C</span>
    </p>

    <div class="phase-poem-stage">
      <span class="phase-poem-zero">0&deg;</span>

      <div class="phase-poem-cube">
        <span>NOTHING</span>
        <span>NOTHING</span>
        <span>NOTHING</span>
        <span>NOTHING</span>
        <span>NOTHING</span>
        <span>NOTHING</span>
        <span>NOTHING</span>
      </div>

      <div class="phase-poem-drift">
        <span>N</span>
        <span>O</span>
        <span>T</span>
        <span>H</span>
        <span>I</span>
        <span>N</span>
        <span>G</span>
      </div>

      <div class="phase-poem-puddle">
        <span>THE WORK</span>
        <span>WAS HAPPENING</span>
        <span>ALL ALONG</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="phase-poem-readout">
      <span>THE READING IS FLAT.</span>
      <strong>THE STRUCTURE IS NOT.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>

  <figcaption class="phase-poem-caption">
    <strong>UNCHANGED IS NOT UNTOUCHED.</strong>
    Under ordinary conditions, ice can look unchanged from &minus;5&deg;C to
    0&deg;C while absorbing energy. During melting, the reading can stay near
    0&deg;C while still more energy changes its structure.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

